From: WiFiGUY512 <339406050+WiFiGUY512@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: place CALDB in the fixed host memory region

When "memory-region" provides fixed host memory, QCN9074 still receives
CALDB paddr 0 because coldboot_cal_mm is false for it. On the Arista
C-360 (IPQ8074 + 2x QCN9074) the firmware then never answers the QMI
target capability request after FW_MEM_READY. Place CALDB directly after
HOST_DDR inside the reserved region whenever that region exists, as is
already done when cold boot calibration is enabled.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c	2026-10-06 20:06:21.554691423 -0500
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c	2026-10-06 20:06:21.570691606 -0500
@@ -2088,7 +2088,14 @@
 				return -EINVAL;
 			}
 
-			if (ath11k_core_coldboot_cal_support(ab)) {
+			/*
+			 * With a fixed host memory region, place CALDB right after
+			 * HOST_DDR inside it even when cold boot calibration is not
+			 * used. Handing QCN9074 a CALDB address of 0 (no RAM there on
+			 * IPQ807x) leaves its firmware silent after FW_MEM_READY.
+			 */
+			if (ath11k_core_coldboot_cal_support(ab) ||
+			    res.flags != IORESOURCE_UNSET) {
 				if (res.flags != IORESOURCE_UNSET) {
 					ab->qmi.target_mem[idx].paddr =
 							res.start + host_ddr_sz;
